WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
September 2019.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.910
A global board warns of a rapidly moving,

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.730
highly lethal respiratory pandemic.

4
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.950
It says such a pandemic could
kill 50 to 80 million people,

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.570
and the world is unprepared.

6
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:20.610
Months later, on 31 December 2019, pneumonia
cases are reported in Wuhan, China.

7
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:25.960
By 11 March 2020, WHO
calls COVID-19 a pandemic.

8
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:34.070
WHO estimates about 14.9 million
deaths above normal in 2020 and 2021.

9
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.690
Why, when the world was warned?

10
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.370
In this mission, you'll trace how
an outbreak becomes a pandemic,

11
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.170
and why excess deaths and
reported deaths differ.

12
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.990
Then you'll judge the responses, from
South Korea to the 2025 Pandemic Agreement.

13
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.480
Your mission: explain why a warned
world still lost so many lives.
